@startuml ThreadPoolComponentDiagram
title **tp::ThreadPool Component Diagram**
skinparam componentStyle uml2
left to right direction

package "Application" {
    [Producer thread 1] as P1
    [Producer thread 2] as P2
    [Producer thread m] as Pm
    [Caller (holds std::future)] as Caller
}

package "Configuration (tp::Config)" {
    [Built-in defaults] as Defaults
    [Config file\n(threadpool.ini / $TP_CONFIG_FILE)] as File
    [TP_* environment variables] as Env
    [Code\n(fluent setters)] as Code
    [Config::load() / validate()] as Loader
}

package "tp::ThreadPool" {
    () "submit(f, args...)" as Submit
    () "post(f, args...)" as Post
    [Overflow policy\n(block | reject | caller_runs)] as Overflow
    queue "Task queue\n(std::deque, bounded or unbounded)" as Queue
    [Shutdown policy\n(drain | discard)] as Shutdown
    [Stats\n(pending, active, completed,\nfailed, rejected)] as Stats

    package "Workers (1..n)" {
        [Worker 1] as W1
        [Worker 2] as W2
        [Worker n] as Wn
    }
}

Defaults --> Loader : lowest
File --> Loader
Env --> Loader
Code --> Loader : highest
Loader --> Overflow : configures pool

P1 --> Post
P2 --> Post
Pm --> Submit
Caller --> Submit

Submit --> Overflow
Post --> Overflow
Overflow --> Queue : enqueue
Overflow ..> Caller : caller_runs:\nrun inline

Queue --> W1 : dequeue
Queue --> W2 : dequeue
Queue --> Wn : dequeue

W1 ..> Caller : future result /\nexception
W1 ..> Stats
Shutdown ..> Queue : on shutdown()

note bottom of Queue
  Mutex + condition variables
  (notEmpty / notFull / idle).
  waitIdle() blocks until the queue is
  empty and no task is running.
end note
@enduml
